Package: detfield
Title: Detection Fields and Location Surfaces for Acoustic Telemetry
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R:
    person(c("Jacob", "W."), "Brownscombe", , "jakebrownscombe@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-2496-8764"))
Description: Builds detection-efficiency fields for fixed acoustic receiver
    arrays from a fitted range model and distances measured through water, and
    turns detection counts into location surfaces: for each tagged animal and
    time bin, the probability that the animal was in each water cell. The
    surface for a bin is a posterior over water cells from a binomial
    likelihood of the detection counts of every listening receiver, with the
    spread of each receiver's detection probability within a time bin given
    as an argument.
    Credible regions and samples drawn from the surfaces feed habitat and
    movement analyses.
